+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50496356/tennessee-leading-receiver-mike-matthews-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma, boosted by crowd's ire at postponement, beats No. 19 Ole Miss","description":"The Oklahoma crowd let Ole Miss know what they thought of having their game delayed by a day, and the Sooners rode that energy to a 24-17 win over the Rebels.","published":"2026-11-16T00:22:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50495687/sooners-boosted-crowd-ire-postponement-beat-rebels","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4875126/horace-lockett","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Horace Lockett","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Horace Lockett (born July 26, 2004) is an American college football defensive tackle for the UCF Knights. He previously played for the Georgia Tech Yellow Jackets.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Georgia Tech in 2022, Lockett made three appearances. He saw more playing time in the 2023 season and tallied 25 tackles along with 2.5 tackles-for-loss (TFLs) and a forced fumble. However, a hand injury resulted in Lockett being kept out of every game during the 2024 season. The following year, he transferred to the UCF Knights. With UCF, Lockett won a starting role and posted 13 tackles, three TFLs, a sack and two pass breakups. However, a pectoral injury ended his season after four games. Lockett returned for a final season with the Knights in 2026."}]}}